+# Correction #6 reassessment after Phase 2B.4
+
+**Disposition: ACCEPTED for the original structural double-counting correction.**
+This is a source-contract and integration determination, not empirical validation
+of every retained heuristic coefficient or a claim of statistical independence.
+The historical acceptance report remains an accurate record of its earlier
+working tree; this report supplies the subsequent correction and reassessment.
+
+## Evidence supporting the disposition
+
+| Requirement | Implementation / verification |
+| --- | --- |
+| Confirmed duplicate representation receives one numerical base credit | `numerical_evidence.allocate_base_evidence` canonicalizes identical summary instances; registered source keys win ties. Production calculator tests cover both suspicious and benign polarities, repeated aliases and separate equal-valued observations |
+| Pure derived restatement does not add repeated base/domain credit | `evidence_lineage.numerical_restatement_sources` identifies the actual overlap-only fallback, excluding positive contour measurement. Public synthesis regression and the final Midjourney run demonstrate suppression |
+| Restatement cannot regain credit via mechanism terms | `hypothesis_engine.compute_scorecard` delegates both fragment-only positive component terms to `add_fragment_component`; corrected local support feeds the unchanged conversion. Reliable-geometry test gives local support 1.0 and edit 0.18, instead of 1.5 and 0.77 |
+| Descendant contracts reuse lineage and hypothesis scope | Registered restatement descendants require an actually credited ancestor, compatible polarity and identical hypothesis scope. Three descendants add no credit; unavailable required parent produces no new restatement credit |
+| Genuine additional measurements survive | Positive contour topology, mask-relative anomaly intensity, alignment fractions, patch endpoint topology and fresh regional FFT extractions are category C. Regression checks and unchanged Instagram contributions demonstrate preservation |
+| Uncertain shared features are not arbitrarily discounted | Category D surface carry-forward, sensor/CFA, compression, camera multi-role and metadata/OSINT relationships retain their existing coefficients and are documented as empirical uncertainties |
+| Independent-source gates stay lineage-aware | Existing Phase 2B.3 implementation and all its regressions remain intact; shadow/normal synthesis preserves the same corroboration audit |
+| Confidence remains authoritative and hypothesis-specific | Phase 3 policy definitions are unchanged. Adjusted scorecard reaches production evaluation; both final reference route-match sets, primary hypotheses and policy rules remain unchanged |
+| Arithmetic is reconstructable | Extended Phase 2A reconstruction validates eligible base/domain accounting, component suppression and reliability. New corruption tests plus independent final-image replay pass |
+| No shadow activation or unsupported independence claim | Optional shadow starts from corrected production bases, remains diagnostic and cannot overwrite production. Text traces disclose shared ancestry and provisional credit |
+
+Final regression suite: **334 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped**. All original 297
+tests are unchanged. Both complete headless reference pipelines finish with
+zero failed stages and no recorded errors. Full numerical and decision effects
+are in [phase2b4_reference_comparison.md](phase2b4_reference_comparison.md).
+
+## Resolution of the original F01 examples
+
+The prior audit identified confirmed computational overlap and unreconciled
+numerical paths; it explicitly did not prove that every child contribution was
+wholly redundant. This reassessment examines the actual additional properties
+rather than adopting the diagnostic downstream-removal ablation.
+
+- Cross plus **fragment fallback** is a confirmed category-B repeat. All three
+  positive fragment contribution paths and its extra weighted domain are now
+  withheld when cross already represents the overlap.
+- Cross plus **positive contour boundary**, focus and patch spatial are category
+  C relationships: connected contour geometry, regional intensity and endpoint
+  topology are separately measured additions. Their original contributions and
+  explicit compound conditions remain. They are not extra independent sources.
+- Local-support conversion appears once in the final edit term. Local support
+  is not also added directly to the suspicious total. The redundant fragment
+  input is removed before conversion; no second aggregate subtraction occurs.
+- Other single-signal multi-role weights, domain categories for retained genuine
+  findings, surface carry-forward and camera/provenance moderation have explicit
+  existing scoring roles or uncertain conditional value. No identical numerical
+  operation or demonstrably information-free representation remains identified
+  in those reviewed paths. Their effectiveness is an empirical question, not
+  permission to invent a discount or delete every shared-parent contribution.
+
+On this evidence, no **known category A/B numerical defect identified in the
+review remains uncorrected**. Full acceptance depends on these current source
+contracts; a future detector or changed classifier must revisit its equivalence
+contract and add appropriate regression coverage. The acceptance does not mean
+that arbitrary independently copied, unregistered summaries have authenticated
+observation identity: lacking a source contract, equality is insufficient to
+erase potentially distinct measurements.
+
+## Remaining limitations and roadmap consequence
+
+Conditional information gain, statistical correlations and the magnitude of
+existing multi-role effects remain unmeasured. Positive localization/contour
+credit is retained at the existing heuristic weights, not presented as a
+calibrated likelihood increment. Two reference images cannot establish tier
+accuracy, false-positive rates or statistical independence. These are genuinely
+empirical uncertainties under the task's category-D preservation rule.
+
+No detector output, scoring coefficient, detection/routing/mask threshold,
+confidence-policy definition, dependency or GUI/packaging behavior was changed.
+The audit's nonblocking overflow, inactive malformed-detail and unsupported
+partial-route issues are not resolved or concealed by this task.
+
+With correction #6 accepted on the reviewed source contracts, the original
+ten-correction roadmap has no remaining identified structural blocker. This
+targeted reassessment does not repeat the independent audits of the other nine
+corrections, and does not assert broader forensic validation. No commit or push
+was performed.
